## Towards v1.0 (Januray 2026 and later)

- Existing core: improvements
  - [ ] use estimator including pixel-variance by default in the examples
  - [ ] allow multiple GPU workers to work on the same GPU, seeds to be revised accordingly
  - [ ] independent scripts/interface for post-processing samples (more flexibility to create estimates when changing only burn-in, ...), see `pnp` branch

- New core features
    - [ ] MML (marginal maximum likelihood features, based on older codes already available internally)
    - Langevin-based kernels:
        - [ ] add prox parameter in __init__, so that it can be taken into account directly in mc_step, and not rewritten each time in the implementation of prox (prox_step = step_size * prox_parameter)?
        - [ ] add default method to compute step-size from Lipschitz constant?
        - [ ] diffusion-based samplers (Coeurdoux and others, ...)
        - [ ] additional inverse problems (ORION-B, PDEs, meshes, ...)

- Management, backends and build
  - [ ] build support for 'win-64' 'osx-64' 'osx-arm64' for the dependencies considered (per-platform requirements in `pyproject.toml`)
  - [ ] adding new GPU backend for Apple plateforms : [mlx](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx), see example here
  - [ ] investigate [onnx](https://github.com/onnx/onnx) for network weights

- Documentation
  - [ ] getting started (doc sphinx), install, tuto
  - setup / versioning
  - [ ] documentation deployment with [Github pages](https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/tutorial/deploying.html)
  - [ ] badges: generate custom badges, see [https://pypi.org/project/badges-gitlab/](https://pypi.org/project/badges-gitlab/) or [https://github.com/sgaunet/gobadger](https://github.com/sgaunet/gobadger)
  - [ ] revise writing for the tutorial + display in the sphinx documentation
  - enhance documentation: https://realpython.com/documenting-python-code/#docstring-formats
  - [ ] proper typing, possibly with [`mypy`](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/existing_code.html) or `pyright`, or [ty](https://github.com/astral-sh/ty), more recent
   - Refs:
    - https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html
    - https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/cheat_sheet_py3.html
    - Example setup: https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/config_file.html#config-file
  - [ ] complete pipeline for versioninig with [`bumpver`](https://github.com/mbarkhau/bumpver), see also https://realpython.com/pypi-publish-python-package/
